WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:02.530
- What would happen if
you would lose your job?

00:00:02.530 --> 00:00:04.830
would you still be able to pay your bills

00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:06.440
and provide for your family?

00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:07.800
Just a couple of years ago,

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:10.490
for me, the answer would've been no.

00:00:10.490 --> 00:00:11.323
I worked in consulting,

00:00:11.323 --> 00:00:14.040
where I surely couldn't
complain about my salary.

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:15.500
If I would've lost that job,

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:18.530
I would've had a big problem
because that was by far

00:00:18.530 --> 00:00:20.720
but most significant income stream.

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:22.250
Thankfully, over the last years

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:25.250
I was able to break free
from this dependency

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:27.370
on only relying on one stream of income.

00:00:27.370 --> 00:00:29.160
So in this video, I
wanna give you an insight

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:31.100
into my journey, into what I did.

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:32.610
So, welcome to another coffee break,

00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:34.480
here on my channel, Firm Learning.

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:36.220
My name is Heinrich, and on my channel

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:38.320
I want to help you to become successful

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:40.230
in the first years of your career.

00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:42.030
So in this video, I'm
first going to show you

00:00:42.030 --> 00:00:44.410
the income streams that
I build for myself.

00:00:44.410 --> 00:00:45.840
And second, some tips

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:48.150
how you can do similar things as well

00:00:48.150 --> 00:00:49.030
that makes sense to you.

00:00:49.030 --> 00:00:50.740
I recently read several articles,

00:00:50.740 --> 00:00:52.710
the claim that an average millionaire

00:00:52.710 --> 00:00:56.100
has about seven incomes
streams to his or her disposal.

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:58.740
So this motivated me to look
into my income streams as well,

00:00:58.740 --> 00:01:00.350
and it turns out that I also have

00:01:00.350 --> 00:01:01.960
seven income streams at the moment.

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:03.660
Unfortunately, I'm no millionaire.

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:06.620
And the truth is also that
it wasn't always like that,

00:01:06.620 --> 00:01:08.880
this is only something that
I did over the last years.

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:11.310
So if we look back into 2019,

00:01:11.310 --> 00:01:14.626
what my situation was then,
I was working in consulting

00:01:14.626 --> 00:01:19.626
and 98% of my income was derived
from this consulting job.

00:01:20.360 --> 00:01:21.300
Already at that time,

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:23.020
before I even started this YouTube channel

00:01:23.020 --> 00:01:24.380
I had some online courses,

00:01:24.380 --> 00:01:27.160
on topics like communications
and slide writing skills,

00:01:27.160 --> 00:01:29.520
and I was earning a handful of extra bucks

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:30.830
by selling these courses.

00:01:30.830 --> 00:01:33.970
But as you can see, I was still
heavily relying on my job.

00:01:33.970 --> 00:01:36.530
Thankfully, the situation
improved already in 2020,

00:01:36.530 --> 00:01:38.820
I was making about a quarter of my income

00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:41.130
not from my full-time regular employment.

00:01:41.130 --> 00:01:42.980
And in 2021, I managed derive,

00:01:42.980 --> 00:01:46.490
almost two-third of my income
outside of my regular job.

00:01:46.490 --> 00:01:48.130
And this is true, even though until today

00:01:48.130 --> 00:01:50.240
I still work in a full-time job

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:52.450
and also with a healthy
development of my salary.

00:01:52.450 --> 00:01:54.300
So how did I make this work for myself?

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:57.150
And for that, let's deep
dive into my income in 2021.

00:01:57.150 --> 00:01:58.910
What's probably surprising is the income

00:01:58.910 --> 00:02:00.740
that I derived from my full-time job.

00:02:00.740 --> 00:02:02.050
So after having worked at McKinsey

00:02:02.050 --> 00:02:04.020
for about six years in consulting,

00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:06.090
I now work as chief revenue officer

00:02:06.090 --> 00:02:08.590
for a Munich-based property
technology company.

00:02:08.590 --> 00:02:11.710
But let's now also talk about
the other six income streams.

00:02:11.710 --> 00:02:13.530
And I wanna start by the income streams

00:02:13.530 --> 00:02:16.100
that are most closely related
to the YouTube channel.

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:18.110
Because fun fact,
whenever you tell someone

00:02:18.110 --> 00:02:19.460
